 to return for the  sequel  which also features a series of  harrowing scenes of addiction and  recovery as doyle is captured by  charnier  and injected with heroin as an  interrogation tactic  by the time charnier lets him go popeye  doyle is a full-blown  addict and must go cold turkey in a  french police station holding cell  it's not exactly a barrel of laughs the  third film to pick up the story is  called popeye doyle and stars ed o'neill  as the title character  the movie was made for television and  seemed designed as the launching point  for a television show but  the spin-off series never really  happened still  even if it was more of a tv pilot popeye  doyle was clearly  established as a further story following  the same character from the first two  films  so it certainly counts as the third  installment in the trilogy  [Music]  one of the all-time great monster movies  the creature from the black lagoon  introduced the world to the gill man the  scaliest member of the universal  monsters roster  and like his equally iconic cohorts old  gilly  inspired a franchise that would inspire  both fear  and pity in this prehistoric fiend the  whole concept of the gill man began when  producer william allen  attended a dinner party at orson welles  house there he met a cinematographer who  told the story of a reptilian monster  that lived in the amazon  and occasionally kidnapped native women  this bizarre anecdote inspired  a spark in allent who went on to make  that famous first film  which is about a troupe of explorers who  traveled to south america and encounter  an amphibious beast with a thing for  women in bathing suits  the movie was released in 3d a  revolutionary innovation at the time  and turned out to be an immediate hit  and before production had even finished  universal was already setting up the  next entry in a new series  the follow-up was titled revenge of the  creature and  in this film the gill man is captured  put on display  and tortured by scientists soon enough  however he escapes and our fishy friend  decides to go looking  for revenge things then get super weird  in the final film  the creature walks among us in this  entry the gill man is set on fire and  most of his skills are burned off then  after undergoing surgery the creature  comes out  looking incredibly human-like the rest  of the film follows the gill man  as he tries to adjust the human world  all the while  dreaming of his home beneath the water  it's  not great the 2010 sci-fi action film  skyline  is less a piece of cinema and more a  truly wild  over-the-top thrill ride it stars eric  balfour  and scotty thompson as jared and lynn a  married couple with a baby on the way  who attend a friend's birthday party as  aliens suddenly invade the los angeles  the film has a truly strange ending too  in which jared and elaine  are captured and taken aboard an alien  ship where jared's brain is extracted  from his body and  placed into a biomechanical alien body  you know  for reasons but jared's brain suddenly  glows red instead of blue like the other  alien drones  which apparently means he has retained  his memories and  personality the movie ends with the  alien jared protecting his still human  wife  and unborn child from the other aliens  incredibly things get  even stranger and beyond skyline a  follow-up flick in which elaine's  pregnancy is accelerated  as is the growth of the daughter to whom  she gives birth  along the way a resistance movement  against the aliens begins to come  together including other alien drones  who managed to maintain their inner  humanity just as  jared did the third movie in the trilogy  skylines  finds humanity and their half-human  allies finally managing to defeat the  aliens ten years later  under the leadership of jared and  elaine's fully grown ten-year-old  daughter  director liam o'donnell helmed all three  movies so there does appear to be  some kind of artistic vision at work  here no matter how little sense  it seems to make check out one of our  newest videos right here plus even more  looper videos about your favorite movies  are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss  a single one
 

